# Cubeless clouds — original RXSkySystem style

## Dusk-to-night handoff follow-up

Night readability now runs after dusk grading, preventing the later dusk blend
from suppressing the added night fill. Colour and opacity share a smooth -6° to
-45° solar-elevation transition. Full daylight and deep-night endpoints remain
unchanged. The BP palette times and other scene settings were not retuned.

Editor screenshots at 18:30, 19:00, 19:30, 20:00, 20:30 and 21:00 are in `Dusk/`.
The editor was left at 20:00 for review without saving the user's dirty map.
The material passed native cold load and SM6 cook with UnrealMCP disabled (zero
errors, two existing Lumen priority warnings). Full verification passed 42/42
with 7,027 unchanged candidate inputs; the final material matches the frozen
hash. See [verification evidence](Dusk/Verification/verification_summary.json).

## Night readability follow-up

The owned cloud shader now preserves a blue minimum night luminance, shaped by
coverage and moon-facing transport, and retains 0.75 deep-night opacity instead
of 0.42. Daylight terms, celestial holdout and fog support remain intact. The
editor was left at midnight for review, with the user's unsaved level edits
retained; only the material was saved. Character and world lighting were not raised.

![Night cloud readability](Night/after.png)

The previous almost invisible result is recorded in `Night/before.png`. Cloud
motion remains active, so these are visual comparisons rather than pixel metrics.
Cold native load and SM6 cook with UnrealMCP disabled passed; cook reported zero
errors and the two existing Lumen priority warnings. Fresh full verification
passed 42/42 with 7,027 unchanged candidate inputs. The shader comparison confirms
only the two night terms changed, ignoring comment indentation. Evidence is in
[Night verification](Night/Verification/verification_summary.json).

## Height-fog follow-up

The owned cloud instance now uses `M_Cubeless_Clouds_Fog`, duplicated from the
original RX cloud material with Apply Fogging enabled and per-pixel fog retained.
The live MID resolves to this material. Original RX material bytes are unchanged;
the user's unsaved map edits, fog values and placement were not saved or replaced.
Foreground volumetric fog can now also overlay clouds, as requested.

The updated assets passed native cold load and SM6 cook with UnrealMCP disabled
(zero cook errors, two existing Lumen priority warnings), plus a fresh 42/42 full
profile over 7,027 unchanged candidate inputs. See [fog evidence](Fog/Verification/verification_summary.json).
The before/after images include ongoing cloud animation and are visual records,
not a matched-pixel measurement of fog strength.

The new `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_Cubeless` level copies the
user's saved RX preview and replaces only its cloud source with an owned native
RX channel package. The original RX preview/assets and previous BC7 baking
preview are preserved. The editor is left on the new copy at the user's original
11.51999855 time of day and camera direction; automatic cloud movement remains on.

The original RX palette dome, painterly cloud lighting, shadow material, fog,
time controls and review game mode remain in use. The separate copied Blueprint
references owned cloud/shadow instances, including its runtime MID creation paths.
This is a baked dome representation, with no runtime VDB or volumetric-cloud actor.

