## Channels and authoring

A new 2K native bake captures the RX ring at 20° elevation, zenith, nadir,
four horizon directions and coverage: 528 actual scene captures. Positive RGBA
stores ring 0°, ring 90°, zenith and coverage; Negative RGBA stores ring 180°,
ring 270°, nadir and mean horizon lighting. Negative alpha is never treated as
opacity. Transport gain four is retained and the cloud instance's baked phase
anisotropy is zero. This is a fresh directional capture, not an approximation
expanded from the earlier three-channel BC7 data.

Both packs receive the same coverage-controlled offline edge filter. They remain
linear 2K HDR with alpha, trilinear filtering and full resident mip chains. No
additional runtime filter taps were added. The HDR pair is approximately 85 MiB
with mips; a smaller compressed delivery format is a separate possible follow-up.
Fine wisps retain some source texture, and the original RX transport basis still
interpolates between fixed directions rather than doing live volume lighting.

See the [editable asset paths and controls](../../../MCPGameProject/Content/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/README.md).
The two Python authoring changes are the optional 2K native-pair output and
`rxsky_pair_package.py`. No project or plugin C++ was changed.

## Validation

- Capture completed and restored light, source material and quality state.
- Native Blueprint reference remap and copied-map actor replacement passed.
- Current editor daytime and sunset renders use the owned cloud material.
- Cold UE 5.6.1 load with UnrealMCP disabled passed; native `UpdateSky` checked
  11:31, 17:30, 20:00 and 00:00. Cloud and shadow textures retained their bindings.
- Runtime hard/soft dependency closure contains no UnrealMCP, Cloud_VDB,
  CubelessClouds authoring source or RXSkyBaking assets. The inherited review
  game mode retains its existing character/game dependencies.
- Windows SM6 map cook with UnrealMCP disabled passed: zero errors and two
  existing Lumen CVar priority warnings. No full game packaging or PIE claim.
- Full offline profile passed 42/42 in the owned detached candidate with
  7,026 before/after input hashes unchanged. All 37 current-task files matched
  the frozen candidate. Concurrent unrelated changes were excluded.
- Original RX binary asset hashes are unchanged from task start; new binaries
  contain no serialized MCP markers. Images have opaque alpha.

Evidence is in [Verification](Verification/final_summary.json). No commit or push
was performed for this integration.
